    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "overview",
      "narration_text": "On October seventeenth I asked for every remaining video as soon as possible. The count turned out to be thirty-one storyboards, not twenty-nine, so twenty-one concepts were left. Claude Code ran four parallel agents from one shared brief, and by October eighteenth all thirty concepts were built.",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk916",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "The build,",
            "topic": "MEDHAVY · PROGRESS UPDATE",
            "segment": "Build Everything",
            "command": "build --all --remaining",
            "runningText": "planning...",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "Count fixed: 31 storyboards, not 29",
              "21 concepts were left",
              "4 agents, 1 shared brief"
            ],
            "largeText": true
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-25T18:58:52.249806+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 18.99,
      "render_duration_s": 19.0,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeComposerAsk916",
        "at": "2026-10-25T15:32:43"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "point-1",
      "narration_text": "I approved portrait at thirty frames per second, since sixty was wasted, and GPU encodes for 4K. GPU narration, about six and a half times faster, sounds the same to me, but isn't identical, so it's opt-in, and never mixed within one video.",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk916",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "The speed,",
            "topic": "MEDHAVY · PROGRESS UPDATE",
            "segment": "Faster Renders",
            "command": "render --fps 30 --encode gpu",
            "runningText": "benchmarking...",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "Portrait at 30 fps, not 60",
              "4K encodes on the GPU",
              "GPU narration: 6.5x, opt-in"
            ],
            "largeText": true
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 17.07,
      "render_duration_s": 17.1,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-10-25T15:32:43"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "point-2",
      "narration_text": "Running everything at once crashed the Linux side several times, so renders, narration and encodes got locks that allow one of each at a time. Then an API rate limit stopped all four agents, and they were resumed from their saved work.",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk916",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "The limits,",
            "topic": "MEDHAVY · PROGRESS UPDATE",
            "segment": "What Pushed Back",
            "command": "run jobs --parallel",
            "runningText": "crashing...",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "Too many jobs crashed the Linux side",
              "Locks: one render, one encode",
              "Rate limit stopped all 4 agents"
            ],
            "largeText": true
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.53,
      "render_duration_s": 15.533333333333333,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-10-25T15:32:43"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "point-3",
      "narration_text": "Later in the week I said the intro and outro felt abrupt, then that the intro was disjointed. Claude Code measured the frames and audio, and found the question starting while the logo still faded, and the intro's sound cut off. A new recipe holds the logo, fades the sound, and dissolves through white. Twenty-three Shorts were re-stitched.",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk916",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "The polish,",
            "topic": "MEDHAVY · PROGRESS UPDATE",
            "segment": "Smoother Intro",
            "command": "stitch --intro --white-lead-in",
            "runningText": "measuring...",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "Feedback: tight, abrupt, disjointed",
              "Fix: white lead-in, longer dissolves",
              "23 Shorts re-stitched"
            ],
            "largeText": true
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-25T19:02:34.095030+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 20.84,
      "render_duration_s": 20.866666666666667,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeComposerAsk916",
        "at": "2026-10-25T15:32:43"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "point-4",
      "narration_text": "Five Shorts went live, with descriptions written for all twenty-four that were waiting. Their code went into the repo, but the first push hung for twenty-four minutes, waiting for a GitHub login that this clone doesn't have, so it was pushed once with the stored Windows login.",
      "voice": "bm_george",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "remotion": {
